 "sheet": [
  "Write in modern standard Arabic of the quality press (Asharq Al-Awsat, Al-Ahram, Al-Arabiya): clean, plain, no dialect words and no saj' (rhymed ornament).",
  "Open a news item with the fact: who did what, where and when, in the first sentence. A verbal sentence (فعلية) leads: \"أعلنت وزارة المالية القبرصية أمس...\" not \"يعد إعلان وزارة المالية...\"",
  "Prefer the verbal sentence (verb first, subject after) for news and narrative; use the nominal sentence (اسمية) for definitions, descriptions and emphasis. Do not string three nominal sentences in a row.",
  "Replace \"يتم + مصدر\" and \"تم القيام بـ\" with a real active verb and a named subject: \"افتتحت البلدية\" not \"تم افتتاح\"; use the passive (الفعل المبني للمجهول: افتُتح) only when the actor is unknown or irrelevant.",
  "Choose the concrete verb over \"قام بـ / يقوم بـ + masdar\": \"وقّعت الشركة\" not \"قامت الشركة بالتوقيع\".",
  "Avoid \"يعد / يعتبر / يمثل\" as a substitute for \"هو / هي\": say \"هو أكبر منتجع في ليماسول\" and let the number prove it.",
  "Rotate attribution verbs naturally: قال، أوضح، أفاد، أكد، لفت، أشار، ذكر، أضاف، شدد، رأى، كشف. Do not repeat the same one in consecutive sentences, and do not use \"أشار إلى أن\" more than once a paragraph.",
  "Attribute to a named person, institution, document or date: \"قال المدير العام لشركة كذا، أندرياس ...\" — never \"يقول الخبراء\" or \"تشير الدراسات\". If there is no source, drop the claim.",
  "Use the Arabic comma ، semicolon ؛ and question mark ؟ everywhere in Arabic prose; never Latin , ; ?. No space before these marks, one space after.",
  "Use Western digits 0-9 consistently (the site standard), never Arabic-Indic ٠-٩ in the same text. Thousands with a comma and the currency after the number: 1,200 يورو؛ 2.5 مليون يورو؛ 15%.",
  "Write currency in words after the figure (\"350 ألف يورو\", \"1,200 يورو شهريًا\"), not \"€350k\" or \"EUR\". Keep one convention within the piece.",
  "Dates: day month year in Gregorian form, \"12 مارس 2026\" or \"12 آذار/مارس\" consistently; for Gulf readers use the Gregorian month names common in the Gulf (يناير، فبراير، مارس) and keep the same set throughout.",
  "Use « » for quotations and titles, consistently; do not mix with straight \" \". Put the attribution verb in the same sentence as the quote.",
  "Do not use the em dash as a pause: use the comma ، the colon or a new sentence. Parentheses only for a gloss or a number.",
  "Do not use tashkeel (diacritics) or tatweel (ـ) in press text; spell hamza and alef correctly (أ إ آ ؤ ئ ء) and ta marbuta (ة) vs ha (ه) with care.",
  "Cut throat-clearing: no \"من الجدير بالذكر\" or \"تجدر الإشارة إلى أن\". If the fact matters, state it; if not, delete it. Allow at most one such formula per article.",
  "Never close with a moral or a summary (\"في الختام\"، \"خلاصة القول\"). End on the last concrete fact, a date still to come, a price, a quote or an open question the reader can act on.",
  "Avoid \"ليس مجرد ... بل\" and \"ليس فقط ... بل أيضًا\"; state the real point once. Where a contrast is true, name both sides with facts.",
  "Do not build triplets by reflex (أصالة وحداثة وفخامة). Use two items or four, or one precise item.",
  "Vary connectors; most sentences need none. Do not open consecutive paragraphs with علاوة على ذلك، إضافة إلى ذلك، من ناحية أخرى، كما أن. Use a time, place or subject to start instead.",
  "Avoid English calques: \"في نهاية المطاف\", \"يلعب دورًا كبيرًا\", \"جوهرة مخفية\", \"رحلة عبر الزمن\", \"تجربة لا تُنسى\", \"موقع استراتيجي\", \"وجهة مثالية\", \"يسلط الضوء على\". Find the Arabic idiom or the plain verb.",
  "No estate-agent or press-release register: no \"فرصة ذهبية\", \"أسلوب حياة فاخر\", \"يسعدنا أن\", \"تفخر الشركة\". Say price, area, floor, year of completion, distance to the sea in metres.",
  "Cyprus stays specific: name the town, district, street, bay or ruling (Limassol, Paphos, Larnaca, Nicosia, Famagusta; the Republic of Cyprus) and avoid \"جزيرة أفروديت\", \"لؤلؤة المتوسط\", \"المياه الفيروزية\".",
  "Write the Greek and Turkish place names in the usual Arabic form (ليماسول، بافوس، لارنكا، نيقوسيا، فاماغوستا) and give the Latin name in brackets once only where the reader may need it for a search or a contract.",
  "Put Latin names, abbreviations and brand names in the Latin script as written (VAT, GDPR, Bank of Cyprus) and keep punctuation outside the Latin run so the line does not jump; do not mix scripts inside one word.",
  "Use measured adjectives: replace ساحر، خلاب، مذهل، فريد، استثنائي with a measurable detail (the year, the size, the price, the number of rooms, the grandmother who runs the kitchen).",
  "Vary sentence length: after a long sentence of two clauses give a short one. A paragraph of identical length is the machine rhythm.",
  "Prefer the construction \"إن\" and \"أن\" sparingly; do not start every sentence with إن or with a masdar. Start with the subject or time word, then the verb.",
  "For business and law, keep the register sober and exact: name the law and the article (قانون الشركات القبرصي، المادة), the authority (دائرة تسجيل الشركات), the deadline and the fee; state what is not yet decided.",
  "For lifestyle desks (food, fashion, travel) allow warmth, not flourish: one sensory detail, a named person or place, a price. No \"نكهات غنية\" or \"إطلالة خلابة\" unless the text describes it.",
  "For interviews: open on a scene or a sharp quote, put the question and answer in the speaker's own words, and use قال/أجاب, never \"أفصح\" or \"كشف النقاب\" for ordinary statements.",
  "Never output assistant chatter, markdown (** or #), placeholders or meta notes. Deliver the finished article only."
 ],
